    "intro_narrative": "The year is 2142, decades after the Great Collapse decimated human civilization. The surface above is an inhospitable wasteland of ash, radioactive storms, and rusting monuments to a forgotten era. You are a lone scavenger, driven by legends of a sanctuary untouched by the fallout. Your journey has brought you deep underground to Sub-Station Echo, a heavily fortified and long-abandoned military bunker. The air inside is stale and tastes of copper, while the failing emergency lights cast long, flickering shadows against the cold steel walls. Rumors suggest this very bunker holds the final coordinates of a functional haven, locked away behind layers of archaic technology and intricate security systems. To uncover the truth and secure your future, you must thoroughly explore the facility, reactivate dormant terminals, and piece together the scattered fragments of data left behind by the last personnel. Your ultimate objective is to extract the definitive records hidden within. With time running out and your air supply steadily dwindling, your survival depends entirely on your ability to decipher the complex network of devices in this remnant of a fallen world.",
    "narrative_style": "post_apocalyptic"
  },
